  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">3i - Investing In Infrastructure (Cambodia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the 3i: Investing In Infrastructure program is to unlock opportunities for economic growth and trade by increasing investment in private sector-led small-scale infrastructure. This will be supported through two outcomes: increased access to utilities and other infrastructure services for households and businesses; and new and improved opportunities for trade-related business and industries. 3i is a flexible program that is working chiefly in the piped, treated water sector, and in energy distribution. 3i works directly with private sector companies that already build and operate infrastructure to facilitate co-investment which increases the number of households and businesses connected with electricity and piped, treated water.</narrative>
  </description>
